sp("V04-A-005", "Economics and business", "Prices are sticky partly because changing them has costs, though those costs seem too small to explain everything.", "Easy",
   ["Economists have long puzzled over why many prices change so rarely, even when the costs behind them move every week.",
    "One explanation points to the costs of changing a price itself.",
    "Each such cost is small, but if a firm expects the change in its own costs to be temporary, even a small expense can make waiting the sensible choice.",
    "The puzzle does not disappear entirely, however, because the sums involved often look far too small to explain the delays observed.",
    "A second explanation therefore looks to customers rather than to firms: people may resent frequent price changes and take their business elsewhere.",
    "On this account, a stable price is part of what a firm sells."],
   "A restaurant that raises the price of a single dish must reprint its menus, and a shop must relabel its shelves and explain the change to regular customers.",
   [0, 2, 3, 5],
   "The missing sentence gives examples of the cost of changing a price. It must follow the claim it illustrates, 'the costs of changing a price itself', and come before 'Each such cost is small', which refers back to the examples. That is gap (2).",
   {0: "At gap (1) no question about prices has been raised, so the restaurant and the shop would be examples of nothing.",
    3: "At gap (3) the examples would come after the judgement that such costs are small and after the argument about waiting, separating them from the claim they illustrate; 'Each such cost' reads naturally only once particular costs have been listed.",
    5: "At gap (4) the paragraph is discussing customers' resentment, the second explanation; reprinting menus illustrates the first explanation, about firms' own costs."},
   "Placing the examples at gap (3), just before the doubt about whether the costs are large enough.",
   "V04A-menu-costs", "An example after a claim, locked by 'Each such cost'.",
   cognitive="Understanding")

