sp("V04-A-007", "Philosophy and ethics", "Moral luck exposes a conflict between the principle of control and our actual practice of blame.", "Difficult",
   ["Two drivers take the same corner too fast on the same wet evening, and both are equally careless.",
    "One reaches home without incident; a child steps into the road in front of the other.",
    "We blame the second driver far more severely, and so, in all likelihood, does he.",
    "One response is to call our reaction an error: the two are equally guilty, and the second is merely unluckier.",
    "This keeps the principle of control intact, but at a cost, for it asks us to treat the grief and remorse of the second driver as a kind of confusion.",
    "Another response accepts that luck shapes what we are answerable for, and concludes that the principle was never as firm as it seemed.",
    "Neither response is comfortable, and the discomfort is itself the discovery: our practice of blame rests on two commitments that do not fit together."],
   "Yet if blame should track only what lies within a person's control, this difference is hard to justify, since the child's step was no doing of his.",
   [3, 4, 5, 7],
   "The missing sentence states the puzzle: our harsher blame of the second driver ('this difference') clashes with the idea that blame tracks only control. It must follow the observation that we blame him more, and it must come before 'One response', which needs a problem to respond to, and before 'the principle of control', which the paragraph treats as already introduced. Only gap (1) satisfies both links.",
   {4: "At gap (2) the first response has already declared our reaction an error, so raising the puzzle now is backwards, and it separates 'This keeps the principle of control intact' from the response that 'This' refers to.",
    5: "At gap (3) the paragraph has already explained what the first response costs; restating the puzzle here interrupts the pairing of the two responses and leaves 'One response' earlier with nothing to respond to.",
    7: "At gap (4) the paragraph has already concluded that the two commitments do not fit together; posing the puzzle after its own resolution reverses the argument."},
   "Placing the sentence at gap (2), next to 'the principle of control', because it mentions control.",
   "V04A-moral-luck", "The missing sentence shares the word 'control' with a later sentence, which pulls weaker solvers to gap (2); the correct gap follows from seeing that 'One response' and 'the principle of control' both presuppose the puzzle.",
   exams=DX)

