sp("V04-A-011", "Economics and business", "Firms may pay above the market wage because higher pay buys effort, choice and lower turnover, though only where effort is hard to watch.", "Medium",
   ["Standard reasoning suggests that a firm should pay no more than it must, offering the lowest wage at which it can fill its posts.",
    "One reason is that a worker who earns more than she could get elsewhere has more to lose if she is dismissed, and so she has reason to work carefully even when no one is watching.",
    "A better wage also draws more applicants, letting the firm choose among them, and it reduces the cost of training replacements for those who leave.",
    "On this view, a higher wage can pay for itself, since what the firm spends on pay it partly recovers in effort, in selection and in lower turnover.",
    "The argument has a limit, however: it works best where effort is hard to monitor and departures are costly, and where output is easily measured, the lowest wage may still be the sensible choice."],
   "Yet many employers knowingly pay above that level, and they are not simply being generous.",
   [1, 2, 3, 5],
   "'Yet' sets the employers' practice against the standard reasoning, and 'that level' refers to 'the lowest wage at which it can fill its posts'. The sentence also promises a reason other than generosity, and the next sentence begins 'One reason is', which needs a practice to explain. It must therefore follow the opening sentence, at gap (1).",
   {2: "At gap (2) the first reason for paying more has already been given; announcing the puzzling practice after explaining it reverses the order, and 'that level' would no longer point clearly to the lowest wage.",
    3: "At gap (3) the sentence would interrupt the list of reasons and place the fact to be explained in the middle of its explanation.",
    5: "At gap (4) the practice would be introduced only after its reasons and limits, leaving the earlier 'One reason is' with nothing to explain, and the promise that employers are 'not simply being generous' would point to an explanation already given."},
   "Placing the sentence at gap (4), reading it as a closing remark about employers.",
   "V04A-efficiency-wages", "A contrast marker and the reference 'that level' fix the position; the others require only moderate care.")

